+
+/** Reorder `items` to follow `sequence` (a list of slugs), keeping anything the
+ * sequence does not mention in its incoming position at the end.
+ *
+ * A move stages a pending change; it does not rewrite the markdown, which only
+ * happens at publish. So the files still hold the OLD numbers, and re-deriving
+ * the order from them would snap every row back the instant it moved — the
+ * session's arrangement has to be remembered separately and re-applied.
